# Findings accepted individually, by fingerprint.
#
# Each line is commit:file:rule:line for one specific finding. They are all
# inside evals/datasets/gitlab-handbook-v1/source — 200 GitLab Handbook pages
# reproduced verbatim under CC BY-SA 4.0 as an evaluation corpus — and they are
# all documentation examples: `curl -H "Authorization: <token>"` in an API
# runbook, and two lines describing the shape a GitLab Runner token takes.
# GitLab's published docs. Not credentials, not ours, granting access to
# nothing.
#
# Why fingerprints and not a path rule. The first version of this exemption
# allowlisted every Markdown file under every dataset source directory, which
# would have silently swallowed a genuine secret added there later. These six
# lines accept six known findings and nothing else; a seventh fails the build.
#
# The files cannot be edited to remove the matches. test_eval_dataset.py
# verifies them against source/SHA256SUMS and the attribution states they are
# unmodified, so redacting a line to quiet a scanner would falsify that claim.
# The fingerprints are stable for the same reason: those files are immutable by
# design, so their commits, paths and line numbers do not move.

